\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Causal attention mask}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{transformer}
\tag{attention}

\p{For a sequence of length #{n}, the \newvocab{causal attention mask} is
the matrix #{M\in(\{0\}\cup\{-\infty\})^{n\times n}} defined by
##{
M_{ts}=
\begin{cases}
0,&s\leq t,\\
-\infty,&s>t.
\end{cases}
}
Masked attention replaces the score matrix in \ref{ftip-000L} by
#{QK^{\mathsf T}/\sqrt{d_k}+M}.}

\p{The decoder mask in \citet{sec. 3.2.3}{vaswani2017attention} prevents a
position from attending to later output positions. This is a statement about
the attention weights. Prefix non-interference for the complete network also
requires every other operation to respect the positionwise causal data flow.}
